pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% As 09, but the output formula is supplied as a file (4th argument), so the
% checker actively compares its declared `preserved: x1 x2` against its own
% preserved set and reports them equal. Input has 1 solution over {x1}; out.opb
% has 2 over {x1,x2}. Run: veripb --opb pres.opb pres.pbp out.opb
f 1 ;
preserved_add x2 4611686018427387904 x1 >= -4611686018427387904 ;
output EQUIENUMERABLE FILE ;
conclusion ENUMERATION_PARTIAL 0 ;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
